      "raw": "<p>(mild spoilers)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I have a very simple question about all mission/reward cards, that doesn't seem to be addressed in the rulebook.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>When a mission card flips, is the reward put in my hand? Is it put in my play area?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Is the answer different depending on what type it is?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>So far, an internet search has turned up a few posts that hint at rewards going to hand except for targets, and a&nbsp;Kickstarter page from before release&nbsp;that suggests one-shots should go in my hand but all others directly into play. So I'm seeing many different possibilities, and nothing to clarify what rule was actually intended by the designers.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Can someone clarify this for me?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I have to say, I love Sentinels and I'm really looking forward to trying Oblivaeon... I'm just disappointed that such a basic game rule is not covered in the rulebook! I imagine it seems obvious to some, but it is not obvious to me. When a card has so many different states it could be in, it really helps to have a clear explanation of how those states change.&nbsp;</p>",
